      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes. this is not a scaling register.\nrefer to this register\ndatasheet is here\nhttps://b.corp.google.com/issues/182373694#comment16\n\nANA_EN_REG1 (0x21)\n\nbriefly\n0x1001 1011\n\n7th bit - CLS_DISABLE\n6:5 bit - UV_VBAT_SET  \n4th bit - UV_VBAT_EN\n3rd bit - BAT_SHRT_EN\n2:1 bits - OV_VBAT_SET  (01 \u003d 9.2V-9.6V for 2S and 13.5V-14.1V for 3S)\n0 th bit - OV_VBAT_EN \n\nthat is why both have the same value. hardware comparator has +/-5% tolerance.\npreviously when the value was set to (2:1 bits) 00, they were false tripping 2S battery 8.8V-9.2V.",
